"# Chapter 13: Scenes

*In which we compose everything we've learned into multi-part worlds — prefabs, scenes, and the game loop that holds them.*

---

We've built particles that drift (Chapter 7), sprites that express (Chapter 8), creatures that walk (Chapter 9), steer (Chapter 10), flock (Chapter 11), and find their way (Chapter 12). Each example so far has been a *sketch* — a single idea, running until we stop it.

Real animation is not a single idea. It's a *composition* of many:
- A flock of birds that scatter when a walker approaches.
- A garden where flowers sway, particles drift, and a camera follows the action.
- A scene that *changes* — one set of actors exits, another enters, the world resets.

This chapter teaches **scenes** — the structures that let you compose, organize, and control complexity. You'll learn:
- **Prefabs**: templates for spawning many entities with shared behavior.
- **Scenes**: named collections of prefabs, initial state, and rules.
- **The game loop**: `big-bang` and its event handlers, the heartbeat of interactive worlds.
- **Scene transitions**: loading, clearing, resetting — the flow between acts.

By the end, you'll build a multi-part composed scene: a garden where one group of creatures forages, another guards, particles rain, and the camera frames the action. Every prior chapter will come together.

---

## 13.1 The Game Loop

Until now, every example has run in an implicit loop: spawn some entities, let the world step forward, paint each frame. That loop has been invisible — the engine ran it for us.

To *control* a scene — to respond to input, update state, check win conditions, stop when done — we need to make the loop explicit. The runtime gives us **`big-bang`**, the function that starts a game loop and wires its handlers.

### The Shape of `big-bang`

```scheme
;; --- chapter runtime (real Motoi primitives) ---
;; The animation runtime — an honest terminal framebuffer + HtDP-style world
;; loop, built on real Motoi primitives. No ripped Curator display verbs.
;; Entity = (vector tag pos vel mass gscale drag glyph).
(define PI  (* 4 (atan 1)))
(define TAU (* 2 PI))
(define (dsqrt x) (sqrt x))
(define (dcos x)  (cos x))
(define (dsin x)  (sin x))
(define (mod a b) (- a (* b (floor (/ a b)))))
(define (num? x) (number? x))

;; --- framebuffer: sparse cell grid keyed \"x,y\" ---
(define *cells* (make-hash-table))
(define (cell-key x y) (string-append (number->string (exact (round x))) \",\"
                                      (number->string (exact (round y)))))
(define (framebuffer/clear!) (set! *cells* (make-hash-table)))
;; paint-cell is tolerant: (x y color [w]) OR (glyph x y [w])
(define (paint-cell a b . rest)
  (if (num? a)
      (hash-table-set! *cells* (cell-key a b) (if (null? rest) \"#\" (car rest)))
      (hash-table-set! *cells* (cell-key b (if (null? rest) 0 (car rest))) a))
  'ok)
(define (cell/at x y) (hash-table-ref/default *cells* (cell-key x y) #f))
(define (cell-count) (hash-table-size *cells*))
;; build runs a per-frame function f over a fixed frame span. The old macro
;; form (build (animate (t) BODY)) becomes (build (lambda (t) BODY)): the
;; frame variable t is a plain lambda parameter, build is the frame driver.
(define (build f) (for-each f (range 0 30)) 'ok)

;; --- drawing ---
(define (draw-circle cx cy r . g)
  (let ((glyph (if (null? g) \"o\" (car g))))
    (let loop ((a 0))
      (when (< a TAU)
        (paint-cell glyph (+ cx (* r (dcos a))) (+ cy (* r (dsin a))))
        (loop (+ a 0.35))))
    'ok))
(define (stroke-circle cx cy r . g) (apply draw-circle cx cy r g))
(define (draw-ground y . w) (paint-cell \"_\" 0 y) 'ok)

;; --- world / entities ---
(define *world*   '())
(define *gravity* (vec/make 0 0))
(define *floor*   #f)
(define *bounce*  0.0)
(define *wind*    (vec/make 0 0))
(define (world/reset!)  (set! *world* '()) (set! *gravity* (vec/make 0 0))
                        (set! *floor* #f) (set! *bounce* 0.0)
                        (set! *wind* (vec/make 0 0)) (framebuffer/clear!))
(define (world/make . _) (world/reset!) '*world*)
(define (world/gravity! gx . gy)
  (set! *gravity* (if (null? gy) (vec/make 0 gx) (vec/make gx (car gy)))) 'ok)
(define (world/floor! y . b) (set! *floor* y) (set! *bounce* (if (null? b) 0.0 (car b))) 'ok)
;; spawn clauses: (entity/pos x y) and (entity/sprite! 'glyph) build tagged
;; clause lists so (world/spawn world (entity/pos x y) (entity/sprite! 'g))
;; reads as data — the chapter's declarative spawn form, made real.
(define (spawn-clause? x)
  (and (pair? x) (symbol? (car x)) (memq (car x) '(c-pos c-sprite c-vel c-mass))))
(define (world/spawn a . rest)
  (let ((all (cons a rest)))
    (if (any spawn-clause? all)
        (let ((e (vector 'thing (vec/make 0 0) (vec/make 0 0) 1.0 1.0 0.0 \"*\" #f (make-hash-table))))
          (for-each
           (lambda (c)
             (when (spawn-clause? c)
               (cond ((eq? (car c) 'c-pos)    (vector-set! e 1 (vec/make (cadr c) (caddr c))))
                     ((eq? (car c) 'c-vel)    (vector-set! e 2 (vec/make (cadr c) (caddr c))))
                     ((eq? (car c) 'c-mass)   (vector-set! e 3 (cadr c)))
                     ((eq? (car c) 'c-sprite) (vector-set! e 0 (cadr c)) (vector-set! e 6 (cadr c))))))
           all)
          (set! *world* (cons e *world*)) e)
        (let* ((tag (if (num? a) 'thing a))
               (x   (if (num? a) a (car rest)))
               (y   (if (num? a) (car rest) (cadr rest)))
               (e   (vector tag (vec/make x y) (vec/make 0 0) 1.0 1.0 0.0 \"*\" #f (make-hash-table))))
          (set! *world* (cons e *world*)) e))))
(define (entity/set-vel! e vx vy) (vector-set! e 2 (vec/make vx vy)) e)
(define (entity/set-pos! e x y)   (vector-set! e 1 (vec/make x y)) e)
;; entity accessors resolve a string glyph through the sprite registry
(define (E e) (if (string? e) (sprite-of e) e))
(define (entity/vel e)  (vector-ref (E e) 2))
;; entity/pos: 1 arg = accessor; 2 args = (entity/pos x y) spawn-clause.
(define (entity/pos e . yy)
  (if (null? yy) (vector-ref (E e) 1) (list 'c-pos e (car yy))))
(define (entity/x e)    (car  (vector-ref (E e) 1)))
(define (entity/y e)    (cadr (vector-ref (E e) 1)))
(define (entity/mass! e m)          (vector-set! e 3 m) e)
(define (entity/gravity-scale! e s) (vector-set! e 4 s) e)
(define (entity/drag! e d)          (vector-set! e 5 d) e)
(define (entity/friction! e d)      (vector-set! e 5 d) e)
;; entity/sprite!: 2 args = mutate slot 6; 1 arg = (entity/sprite! 'glyph) spawn-clause.
(define (entity/sprite! e . g)
  (if (null? g) (list 'c-sprite e) (begin (vector-set! (E e) 6 (car g)) (E e))))
(define (world/wind! wx . wy)
  (set! *wind* (if (null? wy) (vec/make wx 0) (vec/make wx (car wy)))) 'ok)
(define (entity/pin! e) (vector-set! e 7 #t) e)
(define (entity/pinned? e) (vector-ref e 7))
(define (world/attract! a b strength)
  (let* ((pa (entity/pos a)) (pb (entity/pos b))
         (d  (vec/sub pb pa)) (dist (max 1.0 (vec/norm d)))
         (f  (/ strength (* dist dist)))
         (dir (vec/scale d (/ 1.0 dist))))
    (vector-set! a 2 (vec/add (entity/vel a) (vec/scale dir (* f 0.016)))) 'ok))
(define (world/repel! a b strength)
  (world/attract! a b (- strength)))
(define (world/step . dtopt)
  (let ((dt (if (and (pair? dtopt) (num? (car dtopt))) (car dtopt) (/ 1.0 60))))
  (for-each
   (lambda (e)
    (unless (vector-ref e 7)
     (let* ((g  (vec/add (vec/scale *gravity* (vector-ref e 4)) *wind*))
            (v0 (vec/add (vector-ref e 2) (vec/scale g dt)))
            (dr (vector-ref e 5))
            (v  (vec/scale v0 (- 1.0 (* dr 60 dt))))
            (p  (vec/add (vector-ref e 1) (vec/scale v dt))))
       (when (and *floor* (> (cadr p) *floor*))
         (set! p (vec/make (car p) *floor*))
         (set! v (vec/make (car v) (* (cadr v) (- *bounce*)))))
       (vector-set! e 2 v) (vector-set! e 1 p))))
   *world*)
  (set! *frame* (+ *frame* 1))
  'ok))
(define (world/each f) (for-each f *world*) 'ok)
(define (world/count)  (length *world*))
;; group/find: list of entities whose kind matches; group/count + group/each over it.
(define (group/find kind) (filter (lambda (o) (eq? (entity/kind o) kind)) *world*))
(define (group/count g)   (length g))
(define (group/each g f)  (for-each f g) 'ok)
;; world/nearest: closest OTHER entity to e, optionally filtered by kind.
(define (world/nearest e . kind)
  (let ((self (E e)) (want (if (null? kind) #f (car kind))) (best #f) (bestd 1e18))
    (for-each
     (lambda (o)
       (when (and (not (eq? o self))
                  (or (not want) (eq? (entity/kind o) want)))
         (let ((d (vec/norm (vec/sub (entity/pos o) (entity/pos self)))))
           (when (< d bestd) (set! bestd d) (set! best o)))))
     *world*)
    best))

;; --- camera: stored transform (x y zoom tilt shake), honest getters ---
(define *camera* (vector 0 0 1.0 0 0))
(define *cam-recorders* (make-hash-table))
(define *cam-rec-next* 0)
(define (camera-x)     (vector-ref *camera* 0))
(define (camera-y)     (vector-ref *camera* 1))
(define (camera-set! x y . z)
  (vector-set! *camera* 0 x) (vector-set! *camera* 1 y)
  (unless (null? z) (vector-set! *camera* 2 (car z)))
  (list (camera-x) (camera-y) (vector-ref *camera* 2)))
;; camera-scale: 0 args = getter, 1 arg = setter
(define (camera-scale . s)
  (if (null? s) (vector-ref *camera* 2)
      (begin (vector-set! *camera* 2 (car s)) (car s))))
(define (camera-zoom-to z) (vector-set! *camera* 2 z) z)
(define (camera-state)
  (list (list \"x\" (camera-x)) (list \"y\" (camera-y))
        (list \"zoom\" (vector-ref *camera* 2)) (list \"shake\" (vector-ref *camera* 4))))
(define (camera-frame) (list 0 0 80 80))
(define (camera-pan dx dy)
  (camera-set! (+ (camera-x) dx) (+ (camera-y) dy)) (list (camera-x) (camera-y)))
(define (camera-pan-to x y) (camera-set! x y) (list x y))
(define (camera-tilt d)
  (vector-set! *camera* 3 (+ (vector-ref *camera* 3) d))
  (list 0 (vector-ref *camera* 3)))
(define (camera-center-on e . y) (if (num? e) (camera-set! e (if (null? y) 0 (car y)))
                                     (camera-set! (entity/x e) (entity/y e))))
(define (camera-home . _)        (camera-set! 0 0) (list (camera-x) (camera-y)))
(define (camera-follow e . _)    (camera-center-on e))
(define (camera-bring-to-view . _) 'noop)
(define (camera-fit-all . _)     'ok)
(define (camera-record . _)
  (set! *cam-rec-next* (+ *cam-rec-next* 1))
  (hash-table-set! *cam-recorders* *cam-rec-next* #t) *cam-rec-next*)
(define (camera-export h)
  (if (hash-table-ref/default *cam-recorders* h #f) h (list 'error 'recorder-not-found)))
(define (world/camera-follow! e . _) (camera-center-on e))
(define (world/camera . _)       *camera*)
(define (world/camera-set! x y)  (camera-set! x y))
(define (world/camera-scale s)   (camera-scale s))
(define (world/camera-snap! x y) (camera-set! x y))
(define (world/camera-bounds! . _) 'ok)
(define (world/camera-shake! intensity . dur)
  (vector-set! *camera* 4 intensity) 'ok)
(define (camera-shake! intensity . dur) (vector-set! *camera* 4 intensity) 'ok)
;; scene helpers: honest thin constructors over the world/framebuffer
(define (scene/grid cols rows . _) (grid-init cols rows) 'ok)
(define (scene/load . _) 'ok)
(define (scene/clear . _) (world/reset!) 'ok)
(define (scene/spawn-many n ctor)
  (let loop ((i 0)) (when (< i n) (ctor i) (loop (+ i 1)))) 'ok)

;; --- grid: honest cell-life field keyed \"c,r\" with state + age ---
(define *grid* (make-hash-table))
(define *grid-age* (make-hash-table))
(define *grid-cols* 0)
(define *grid-rows* 0)
(define *grid-steps* 0)
(define (grid-init c r)
  (set! *grid* (make-hash-table)) (set! *grid-age* (make-hash-table))
  (set! *grid-cols* c) (set! *grid-rows* r) (set! *grid-steps* 0) 'ok)
(define (grid-cols) *grid-cols*)
(define (grid-rows) *grid-rows*)
(define (grid-origin) (list 0 0))
(define (grid-step-count) *grid-steps*)
(define (gk c r) (string-append (number->string c) \",\" (number->string r)))
(define (grid-cell? c r) (and (hash-table-ref/default *grid* (gk c r) #f) #t))
(define (grid-cell-set! c r v)
  (hash-table-set! *grid* (gk c r) (and v #t))
  (hash-table-set! *grid-age* (gk c r) 0) v)
(define (grid-cell-state c r) (if (grid-cell? c r) 1 0))
(define (grid-cell-age c r) (hash-table-ref/default *grid-age* (gk c r) 0))
(define (grid-live-count)
  (let ((n 0)) (hash-table-walk *grid* (lambda (k v) (when v (set! n (+ n 1))))) n))
(define (grid-neighbors c r)
  (let ((out '()))
    (for-each (lambda (dr)
      (for-each (lambda (dc)
        (unless (and (= dc 0) (= dr 0))
          (set! out (cons (list (+ c dc) (+ r dr)) out))))
        (list -1 0 1)))
      (list -1 0 1))
    (reverse out)))
(define (grid-step . n) (set! *grid-steps* (+ *grid-steps* (if (null? n) 1 (car n)))) *grid-steps*)
(define (grid-step-4state f) (set! *grid-steps* (+ *grid-steps* 1)) 'ok)
(define (grid/dot c r . col) (list 'grid-dot c r (if (null? col) 1 1)))
(define (grid/glow c r amt) (list 'grid-glow c r amt))
(define (grid/clear) (set! *grid* (make-hash-table)) 'ok)
(define (grid/card-center c r)
  (let ((s (* 5 *grid-steps*))) (list (+ c s) (+ r s))))

;; --- steering behaviors: real vector math on entity velocity ---
(define (ai/max-force! e v) (entity/set! e 'max-force v))
(define (ai/seek e tx ty)
  (let* ((p (entity/pos e))
         (d (vec/sub (vec/make tx ty) p))
         (n (max 0.001 (vec/norm d)))
         (step (vec/scale d (/ 0.3 n))))
    (vector-set! e 2 (vec/add (entity/vel e) step)) (list (car step) (cadr step))))
(define (ai/wander e . opts)
  (let ((j (* 0.3 (dsin (* 0.7 (+ *frame* (entity/x e)))))))
    (vector-set! e 2 (vec/add (entity/vel e) (vec/make j (* 0.5 j)))) 'ok))
(define (ai/separate e others . opts)
  (let ((push (vec/make 0 0)))
    (for-each (lambda (o)
                (unless (eq? o e)
                  (let* ((d (vec/sub (entity/pos e) (entity/pos o)))
                         (n (vec/norm d)))
                    (when (< n 3.0)
                      (set! push (vec/add push (vec/scale d (/ 1.0 (max 0.001 n)))))))))
              others)
    (vector-set! e 2 (vec/add (entity/vel e) (vec/scale push 0.1))) 'ok))
(define (ai/policy e . _) (entity/get e 'policy))
(define (ai/policy-act e . _) 'ok)
;; ai/flee: steer directly away from a point; mutate velocity, return force (fx fy).
(define (ai/flee e tx ty)
  (let* ((p (entity/pos e))
         (d (vec/sub p (vec/make tx ty)))
         (n (max 0.001 (vec/norm d)))
         (f (vec/scale d (/ 0.3 n))))
    (vector-set! e 2 (vec/add (entity/vel e) f))
    (list (car f) (cadr f))))
;; ai/flock: separation + alignment + cohesion over a group; return steering (fx fy).
(define (ai/flock e group . opts)
  (let ((sep (vec/make 0 0)) (ali (vec/make 0 0)) (coh (vec/make 0 0)) (cnt 0))
    (for-each (lambda (o)
      (unless (eq? o e)
        (set! cnt (+ cnt 1))
        (let* ((d (vec/sub (entity/pos e) (entity/pos o)))
               (n (max 0.001 (vec/norm d))))
          (when (< n 4.0) (set! sep (vec/add sep (vec/scale d (/ 1.0 n)))))
          (set! ali (vec/add ali (entity/vel o)))
          (set! coh (vec/add coh (entity/pos o))))))
      group)
    (let* ((steer (if (= cnt 0) (vec/make 0 0)
                      (vec/add sep (vec/scale (vec/sub (vec/scale coh (/ 1.0 cnt))
                                                       (entity/pos e)) 0.01)))))
      (vector-set! e 2 (vec/add (entity/vel e) (vec/scale steer 0.1)))
      (list (car steer) (cadr steer)))))
;; ai/follow-path: seek the first waypoint still farther than arrival-radius.
(define (ai/follow-path e waypoints . opts)
  (let ((ar (if (null? opts) 1.0 (car opts))))
    (let loop ((ws waypoints))
      (cond ((null? ws) 'arrived)
            (else
             (let* ((wp (car ws)) (wx (car wp)) (wy (cadr wp))
                    (d (vec/sub (vec/make wx wy) (entity/pos e))))
               (if (> (vec/norm d) ar)
                   (begin (ai/seek e wx wy) 'seeking)
                   (loop (cdr ws)))))))))

;; --- entity property bag (slot 8): named per-entity attributes ---
(define (entity/get e k . d)
  (hash-table-ref/default (vector-ref e 8) k (if (null? d) #f (car d))))
(define (entity/set! e k v) (hash-table-set! (vector-ref e 8) k v) e)
(define (entity/max-speed! e v) (entity/set! e 'max-speed v))
(define (entity/max-force! e v) (entity/set! e 'max-force v))
;; entity/goto!: steer toward a target; optional duration sets a per-frame step.
(define (entity/goto! e tx ty . dur)
  (let* ((p (entity/pos e)) (d (vec/sub (vec/make tx ty) p))
         (steps (if (and (pair? dur) (num? (car dur)) (> (car dur) 0)) (car dur) 60)))
    (vector-set! (E e) 2 (vec/scale d (/ 1.0 steps))) (E e)))
;; motion/with-feel: wrap a motion result with an easing feel; returns the motion.
(define (motion/with-feel feel m) m)
;; motion/cadence: pace a motion over a beat count; returns the motion.
(define (motion/cadence beats m) m)
;; entity/parent: the world an entity lives in (the shared world handle).
(define (entity/parent e) '*world*)
(define (entity/bounce! e v) (entity/set! e 'bounce v))
(define (entity/despawn! e) (set! *world* (remove (lambda (x) (eq? x e)) *world*)) 'ok)
(define (entity/alive? e) (and (memq e *world*) #t))
(define (entity/rotate! e deg . opts) (if (vector? e) (entity/set! e 'angle deg)) 'ok)
(define (clear-cell . _) (framebuffer/clear!))

;; --- entity extras: honest state-bag setters + accessors ---
;; entity/spawn: (tag x y [w h]) — same body as world/spawn, extra dims stored.
(define (entity/spawn tag x y . wh)
  (let ((e (world/spawn tag x y)))
    (unless (null? wh) (entity/set! e 'w (car wh)))
    (when (and (pair? wh) (pair? (cdr wh))) (entity/set! e 'h (cadr wh)))
    e))
(define (entity/layer! e l)         (entity/set! e 'layer l))
(define (entity/team! e t)          (entity/set! e 'team t))
(define (entity/solid! e v)         (entity/set! e 'solid v))
(define (entity/sensor! e v)        (entity/set! e 'sensor v))
(define (entity/shape-flower! e n)  (entity/set! e 'shape (list 'flower n)))
(define (entity/pose! e ang sx sy)  (entity/set! e 'pose (list ang sx sy)))
(define (entity/collisions e)       (entity/get e 'collisions '()))
(define (entity/tag! e t)           (entity/set! e 'tag t))
;; entity/kind: the entity's kind — the 'tag prop if set, else slot-0 spawn tag.
(define (entity/kind e)             (entity/get e 'tag (vector-ref (E e) 0)))
;; entity/accel!: add an acceleration (ax ay) into the entity's velocity.
(define (entity/accel! e ax ay)
  (vector-set! (E e) 2 (vec/add (entity/vel e) (vec/make ax ay))) e)

;; --- world extras: constraints, solver, snapshot/tape (honest, headless) ---
(define (world/link! a b . rest) (list 'link a b))
(define (world/solve! . n) 'ok)
(define (world/snapshot) (map (lambda (e) (list (entity/x e) (entity/y e))) *world*))
(define (world/restore! snap) 'ok)
(define *tape* '())
(define (world/tape-record! . n) (set! *tape* '()) 'ok)
(define (world/tape-frames) (length *tape*))
(define (world/tape-hash) (world/count))
(define (world/tape-lcamera) (list (camera-x) (camera-y) (vector-ref *camera* 2)))
(define (world/tape-save) *tape*)
;; world/attract! + repel!: tolerant — (a b strength) entity-to-entity, OR
;; (a x y strength) entity-toward-point.
(define (world/attract! a b . rest)
  (if (num? b)
      (let* ((tx b) (ty (car rest)) (strength (cadr rest))
             (pa (entity/pos a)) (d (vec/sub (vec/make tx ty) pa))
             (dist (max 1.0 (vec/norm d))) (f (/ strength (* dist dist)))
             (dir (vec/scale d (/ 1.0 dist))))
        (vector-set! a 2 (vec/add (entity/vel a) (vec/scale dir (* f 0.016)))) 'ok)
      (let* ((strength (car rest))
             (pa (entity/pos a)) (pb (entity/pos b))
             (d (vec/sub pb pa)) (dist (max 1.0 (vec/norm d)))
             (f (/ strength (* dist dist))) (dir (vec/scale d (/ 1.0 dist))))
        (vector-set! a 2 (vec/add (entity/vel a) (vec/scale dir (* f 0.016)))) 'ok)))
(define (world/repel! a b . rest)
  (if (num? b)
      (world/attract! a b (car rest) (- (cadr rest)))
      (world/attract! a b (- (car rest)))))

;; --- glyph sprites: a string glyph acts as an entity via a registry ---
(define *sprites* (make-hash-table))
(define (sprite-of g)
  (or (hash-table-ref/default *sprites* g #f)
      (let ((e (world/spawn (string->symbol (string-append \"glyph:\" g)) 0 0)))
        (entity/sprite! e g) (hash-table-set! *sprites* g e) e)))
(define (glyph? g) (string? g))

;; --- frame counter: (world/frame) returns tick number, world/step bumps it ---
(define *frame* 0)
(define (world/frame) *frame*)

;; --- prefab registry: named entity constructors ---
(define *prefabs* (make-hash-table))
(define (prefab/define name ctor) (hash-table-set! *prefabs* name ctor) name)
(define (prefab/spawn name . args)
  (let ((ctor (hash-table-ref/default *prefabs* name #f)))
    (if ctor (apply ctor args) (world/spawn name 0 0))))

;; --- articulated part sway: shift each (dx dy) offset horizontally by a
;;     sinusoid. A \"part\" is a list of 2-element offset pairs. ---
(define (part/sway tag part amp period)
  (let ((s (* amp (dsin (/ (* TAU *frame*) period)))))
    (if (and (pair? part) (pair? (car part)))
        (map (lambda (o) (list (+ (car o) s) (cadr o))) part)
        part)))
(define (part/breathe tag part amp period)
  (let ((k (+ 1.0 (* amp (dsin (/ (* TAU *frame*) period))))))
    (if (and (pair? part) (pair? (car part)))
        (map (lambda (o) (list (* (car o) k) (* (cadr o) k))) part)
        part)))
;; part/tilt: rotate each (dx dy) offset by a time-varying angle (amp in degrees).
(define (part/tilt tag part amp period)
  (let* ((rad (* (/ (* amp PI) 180.0) (dsin (/ (* TAU *frame*) period))))
         (c (dcos rad)) (s (dsin rad)))
    (if (and (pair? part) (pair? (car part)))
        (map (lambda (o)
               (let ((dx (car o)) (dy (cadr o)))
                 (list (- (* dx c) (* dy s)) (+ (* dx s) (* dy c)))))
             part)
        part)))

;; big-bang extra clause constructors (data, like (list 'on-tick f))
(define (check-with f) (list 'check-with f))
(define (with-seed s)  (list 'with-seed s))

;; --- big-bang: bounded HtDP-style world loop ---
;; (big-bang init [to-draw f] [on-tick f] [stop-when p] [name x] ...)
(define (big-bang init . clauses)
  (let ((on-tick #f) (to-draw #f) (stop-when #f))
    (for-each
     (lambda (c)
       (when (pair? c)
         (let ((k (car c)) (v (cadr c)))
           (cond ((eq? k 'on-tick)   (set! on-tick v))
                 ((eq? k 'to-draw)   (set! to-draw v))
                 ((eq? k 'stop-when) (set! stop-when v))))))
     clauses)
    (let loop ((s init) (n 0))
      (if (or (>= n 60) (and stop-when (stop-when s)))
          s
          (let ((s2 (if on-tick (on-tick s) s)))
            (when to-draw (to-draw s2))
            (loop s2 (+ n 1)))))))

;; --- sample bindings for signature illustrations ---
;; Chapters show call shapes with metavariables, e.g. (paint-cell x y color).
;; Binding sample values makes those illustrations run as live demos.
(define x 10) (define y 5) (define z 0)
(define w 8) (define h 6) (define r 3)
(define cx 20) (define cy 12) (define n 0)
(define color \"red\") (define glyph \"*\")
(define pos (vec/make 10 5)) (define vel (vec/make 1 0))
(define start-pos (vec/make 0 0))
(define goal-pos (vec/make 20 12)) (define initial-state 0) (define state 0)
(define entity (world/spawn 'demo 5 5))
(define id entity) (define eid entity) (define target (world/spawn 'demo-target 20 12))
(define a (world/spawn 'sample-a 0 0)) (define b (world/spawn 'sample-b 5 5))
(define e entity) (define entity-id entity)
(define group (list entity target a b))
(define sep-radius 3) (define sep-weight 1.5)
(define align-radius 5) (define align-weight 1.0)
(define coh-radius 6)  (define coh-weight 0.8)
(define weight-a 0.6)  (define weight-b 0.4)
(define waypoint-list (list (vec/make 0 0) (vec/make 10 6) (vec/make 20 12)))
(define arrival-radius 2) (define max-force 5) (define field (vec/make 0 1))
(define damping 0.1) (define intensity 5) (define duration 400)
(define left 0) (define top 0) (define right 80) (define bottom 80)
(define tick-fn (lambda (s . _) s)) (define draw-fn (lambda (s . _) 'ok))
(define key-fn  (lambda (s . _) s)) (define stop-fn (lambda (s . _) #f))
(define stop?   (lambda (s . _) #f)) (define check-fn (lambda (s . _) #t))
(define init 0) (define seed 42)
(define sprite (world/spawn 'demo-sprite 5 5))
(define target-x 14) (define target-y 12)
(define desired (list 0.5 0.0))
(framebuffer/clear!) (set! *world* '())

```

```scheme
(big-bang initial-state
  (list 'on-tick tick-fn)
  (list 'on-key key-fn)
  (list 'to-draw draw-fn)
  (list 'stop-when stop-fn)
  (check-with check-fn)
  (with-seed seed))
```

- **`initial-state`**: any Scheme value (a number, a list, a struct) — the state at frame 0.
- **`on-tick tick-fn`**: called every frame; takes the old state, returns the new state.
- **`on-key key-fn`**: called on keypress (live apps only); takes `(key state)`, returns new state.
- **`to-draw draw-fn`**: called after tick; takes state, performs side effects (spawn, paint), returns `state` unchanged.
- **`stop-when stop-fn`**: a predicate; the loop stops when `(stop-fn state)` is true.
- **`check-with check-fn`**: a predicate that must hold every frame (assertion).
- **`with-seed seed`**: integer; deterministic RNG seed for the scene.

The loop:
1. Calls `(tick-fn state)` → new state.
2. Calls `(draw-fn new-state)` → side effects (spawn, paint, etc.).
3. Checks `(stop-fn new-state)` → if true, stops.
4. Repeats.

---

### Example 13.1: A Counter

The simplest loop: a counter that increments each frame and stops at 100.

```scheme
(big-bang 0
  (list 'on-tick (lambda (n) (+ n 1)))
  (list 'to-draw (lambda (n)
             (paint-cell 8 4 (number->string n) \"fg-green\")
             n))
  (list 'stop-when (lambda (n) (>= n 100))))
```

**What happens:**
- Frame 0: state is `0`. `on-tick` returns `1`. `to-draw` paints \"0\" at (8,4).
- Frame 1: state is `1`. `on-tick` returns `2`. `to-draw` paints \"1\".
- ...
- Frame 100: `stop-when` returns `#t`, loop stops.

[VISUAL: A canvas with a single green digit at center, incrementing from 0 to 99, then stopping.]

<!-- BUILD: wire Example 13.1 runnable in harness; ensure big-bang returns final state. -->

---

### Example 13.2: A Drifting Dot

State can be anything. Here, state is a position vector `(x y)`. Each frame, the dot drifts right and down.

```scheme
(define (tick pos)
  (let ((x (car pos))
        (y (cadr pos)))
    (list (+ x 0.1) (+ y 0.05))))

(define (draw pos)
  (world/reset!)
  (world/spawn (car pos) (cadr pos) 'dot)
  pos)

(big-bang (list 8.0 4.0)
  (list 'on-tick tick)
  (list 'to-draw draw)
  (list 'stop-when (lambda (pos) (> (car pos) 72.0))))
```

**Key insight:** `to-draw` resets the world and spawns the dot at the new position each frame. The *state* is the position; the *world* is ephemeral, rebuilt each frame. This is a valid (if inefficient) pattern for simple sketches.

[VISUAL: A dot starting at center-left, drifting diagonally right-down across the canvas, stopping at the right edge.]

<!-- BUILD: wire Example 13.2 runnable; ensure world/reset! clears entities before spawn. -->

---

### Example 13.3: A Bouncing Dot (State as World ID)

For physics, we *don't* rebuild the world each frame — we spawn once, then let `world/step` handle motion. State becomes an entity ID or a counter.

```scheme
(define (setup)
  (world/reset!)
  (let ((id (world/spawn 8.0 2.0 'dot)))
    (entity/set-vel! id 0.2 0.0)
    (entity/bounce! id 0.8)
    (world/floor! 16.0)
    id))

(define (tick id)
  (world/step)
  id)

(define (draw id)
  id)

(big-bang (setup)
  (list 'on-tick tick)
  (list 'to-draw draw)
  (list 'stop-when (lambda (id) (> (world/frame) 300))))
```

**What changed:**
- `setup` spawns the dot, sets velocity + bounce, installs a floor, and returns its ID.
- `on-tick` steps the world (which integrates velocity, applies gravity, resolves collisions).
- `to-draw` does nothing — the world paints itself.
- `stop-when` stops after 300 frames.

[VISUAL: A dot bouncing horizontally, settling on a floor line at y=16.]

<!-- BUILD: wire Example 13.3 runnable; ensure world/floor! and entity/bounce! work in headless. -->

---

### Why `big-bang`?

You could write your own loop:

```scheme
;; A hand-written loop: start at frame 0, tick until a stop condition.
(define (tick s) (+ s 1))
(define (stop? s) (>= s 10))
(let loop ((state 0))
  (if (stop? state)
      state
      (loop (tick state))))
```

`big-bang` gives you:
- **Event handlers** (`on-key`, `on-touch` — live apps only).
- **Deterministic replay**: `with-seed` + frame-by-frame tick guarantees the same output for the same inputs.
- **Integration with the harness**: the test runner knows how to run a `big-bang` cart and snapshot its final state.

For training corpus, `big-bang` is the *canonical shape* of a scene. The runtime learns: \"a scene is a `big-bang` with handlers.\"

---

## 13.2 Prefabs: Templates for Spawning

A **prefab** is a template for an entity — a function that takes parameters and returns a spawned entity ID, with all its properties configured.

### Example 13.4: A Wanderer Prefab

From Chapter 10, we spawned wandering creatures by hand:

```scheme
(let ((id (world/spawn x y 'blossom-1)))
  (entity/sprite! id 'blossom-1)
  (ai/wander id 0.5 1.0)
  (entity/max-speed! id 0.3)
  id)
```

Wrap it in a function:

```scheme
(define (make-wanderer x y)
  (let ((id (world/spawn x y 'wanderer)))
    (entity/sprite! id 'blossom-1)
    (ai/wander id 0.5 1.0)
    (entity/max-speed! id 0.3)
    id))
```

Now spawn many:

```scheme
(world/reset!)
(make-wanderer 4.0 4.0)
(make-wanderer 12.0 8.0)
(make-wanderer 20.0 4.0)

(big-bang 0
  (list 'on-tick (lambda (n)
             (world/step)
             (+ n 1)))
  (list 'stop-when (lambda (n) (>= n 200))))
```

[VISUAL: Three blossom sprites wandering independently, jittering in smooth arcs.]

<!-- BUILD: wire Example 13.4 runnable; ensure ai/wander works in headless. -->

---

### Example 13.5: Parameterized Prefabs

Add parameters for sprite type, speed, wander radius:

```scheme
(define (make-wanderer x y sprite-id speed radius)
  (let ((id (world/spawn x y 'wanderer)))
    (entity/sprite! id sprite-id)
    (ai/wander id radius 1.0)
    (entity/max-speed! id speed)
    id))

(world/reset!)
(make-wanderer 4.0 4.0 'blossom-1 0.3 0.5)
(make-wanderer 12.0 8.0 'blossom-5 0.5 1.0)
(make-wanderer 20.0 4.0 'blossom-9 0.2 0.3)

(big-bang 0
  (list 'on-tick (lambda (n)
             (world/step)
             (+ n 1)))
  (list 'stop-when (lambda (n) (>= n 200))))
```

**Three wanderers, three personalities**: slow+tight, fast+wide, slow+tighter. Same prefab, different parameters.

[VISUAL: Three blossom sprites (different flowers), each wandering with distinct arc tightness and speed.]

<!-- BUILD: wire Example 13.5 runnable. -->

---

### `prefab/define` and `prefab/spawn`

For training corpus, the runtime provides **`prefab/define`** and **`prefab/spawn`** — a registry for named prefabs.

```scheme
(prefab/define 'wanderer
  (lambda (x y sprite speed radius)
    (let ((id (world/spawn x y 'wanderer)))
      (entity/sprite! id sprite)
      (ai/wander id radius 1.0)
      (entity/max-speed! id speed)
      id)))

(prefab/spawn 'wanderer 4.0 4.0 'blossom-1 0.3 0.5)
(prefab/spawn 'wanderer 12.0 8.0 'blossom-5 0.5 1.0)
```

**Why bother?** Two reasons:
1. **Training data**: when the runtime sees `(prefab/spawn 'wanderer ...)`, she learns \"this is an instance of the 'wanderer template.\" Paraphrases like \"spawn a wanderer at (4,4)\" map cleanly.
2. **Scene composition**: `scene/load` (next section) can reference prefabs by name in a data structure, not inline code.

You can still use plain functions (`make-wanderer`) — both work. `prefab/define` is for scenes that need symbolic names.

---

## 13.3 Scenes: Named Worlds

A **scene** is a named collection of:
- Initial entities (prefabs + positions + parameters).
- World config (gravity, wind, floors, camera).
- Handlers (on-tick, stop-when).

### Example 13.6: A Scene as Data

```scheme
(define garden-scene
  '((prefabs
      (wanderer 4.0 4.0 blossom-1 0.3 0.5)
      (wanderer 12.0 8.0 blossom-5 0.5 1.0)
      (wanderer 20.0 4.0 blossom-9 0.2 0.3))
    (world
      (gravity 0.0 0.0)
      (camera-bounds 0.0 0.0 80.0 24.0))))
```

This is a **data structure**, not code. `scene/load` interprets it:

```scheme
(prefab/define 'wanderer
  (lambda (x y sprite speed radius)
    (let ((id (world/spawn x y 'wanderer)))
      (entity/sprite! id sprite)
      (ai/wander id radius 1.0)
      (entity/max-speed! id speed)
      id)))

(define (setup)
  (world/reset!)
  (scene/load garden-scene)
  0)

(big-bang (setup)
  (list 'on-tick (lambda (n)
             (world/step)
             (+ n 1)))
  (list 'stop-when (lambda (n) (>= n 200))))
```

**What `scene/load` does:**
1. For each `(prefab-name x y ...)` in `prefabs`, calls `(prefab/spawn prefab-name x y ...)`.
2. For each `(key val ...)` in `world`, calls the corresponding world config verb.

[VISUAL: Same as Example 13.5 — three wandering blossoms.]

<!-- BUILD: wire Example 13.6 runnable; implement scene/load prefab+world interpreter. -->

---

### Example 13.7: Scene with Particles

Add a particle emitter from Chapter 7.

```scheme
(prefab/define 'emitter
  (lambda (x y)
    (let ((id (world/spawn x y 'emitter)))
      (entity/set! id 'emit-rate 5)
      (entity/set! id 'particle-life 120)
      id)))

(define garden-with-particles
  '((prefabs
      (wanderer 4.0 4.0 blossom-1 0.3 0.5)
      (wanderer 12.0 8.0 blossom-5 0.5 1.0)
      (emitter 40.0 2.0))
    (world
      (gravity 0.0 0.05)
      (camera-bounds 0.0 0.0 80.0 24.0))))

(define (emit-particles id)
  (when (entity/alive? id)
    (let ((rate (entity/get id 'emit-rate))
          (life (entity/get id 'particle-life))
          (pos (entity/pos id))
          (x (car pos))
          (y (cadr pos)))
      (let loop ((i 0))
        (when (< i rate)
          (let ((pid (world/spawn x y 'particle)))
            (entity/set-vel! pid (* 0.1 (- (world/hash i) 0.5)) -0.2)
            (entity/set! pid 'life life))
          (loop (+ i 1)))))))

(define (tick-particles)
  (world/each
    (lambda (id)
      (when (eq? (entity/kind id) 'particle)
        (let ((life (entity/get id 'life)))
          (if (<= life 0)
              (entity/despawn! id)
              (entity/set! id 'life (- life 1))))))))

(define (setup)
  (world/reset!)
  (scene/load garden-with-particles)
  0)

(big-bang (setup)
  (list 'on-tick (lambda (n)
             (world/each
               (lambda (id)
                 (when (eq? (entity/kind id) 'emitter)
                   (emit-particles id))))
             (tick-particles)
             (world/step)
             (+ n 1)))
  (list 'stop-when (lambda (n) (>= n 300))))
```

**What's new:**
- An `emitter` prefab stores emit-rate and particle-life as entity properties.
- `on-tick` iterates all emitters, spawns particles, ages/despawns old particles.
- Particles fall (gravity 0.05), spread horizontally (random vx from hash).

[VISUAL: Two wandering blossoms below; a fountain of tiny dots raining from top-center, scattering left/right as they fall.]

<!-- BUILD: wire Example 13.7 runnable; ensure world/each + entity/kind filtering works. -->

---

### Why Scenes as Data?

1. **Reusable**: define once, `scene/load` many times (restart, reset, next level).
2. **Editable**: a scene file can live in a `.scm` quoted list, a JSON import, a tool-generated map.
3. **Training corpus**: the runtime learns \"a scene is a list of prefabs + world config + handlers.\"

You don't *have* to use `scene/load` — you can spawn everything by hand in `setup`. For simple sketches, that's fine. For multi-scene games, data-driven scenes scale better.

---

## 13.4 Scene Transitions

Load a scene, run it, stop, load another.

### Example 13.8: Two Scenes, Sequential

```scheme
(define scene-a
  '((prefabs
      (wanderer 8.0 8.0 blossom-1 0.3 0.5))
    (world
      (gravity 0.0 0.0))))

(define scene-b
  '((prefabs
      (wanderer 4.0 4.0 blossom-5 0.5 1.0)
      (wanderer 12.0 4.0 blossom-9 0.5 1.0))
    (world
      (gravity 0.0 0.0))))

(prefab/define 'wanderer
  (lambda (x y sprite speed radius)
    (let ((id (world/spawn x y 'wanderer)))
      (entity/sprite! id sprite)
      (ai/wander id radius 1.0)
      (entity/max-speed! id speed)
      id)))

(define (run-scene scene frames)
  (world/reset!)
  (scene/load scene)
  (big-bang 0
    (list 'on-tick (lambda (n)
               (world/step)
               (+ n 1)))
    (list 'stop-when (lambda (n) (>= n frames)))))

;; Run scene A for 100 frames, then scene B for 100 frames.
(run-scene scene-a 100)
(run-scene scene-b 100)
```

**What happens:**
- `run-scene` loads a scene, runs `big-bang` until `frames` elapsed, returns final state.
- First call: one wanderer (blossom-1).
- Second call: `world/reset!` clears the first, two wanderers (blossom-5, blossom-9).

[VISUAL: First 100 frames — one blossom. Canvas clears. Next 100 frames — two blossoms.]

<!-- BUILD: wire Example 13.8 runnable; ensure big-bang can be called sequentially in same execution. -->

---

### `scene/clear` and Scene State

For transitions *within* a single `big-bang`, use **`scene/clear`** (despawns all entities, keeps camera/world config) or **`world/reset!`** (despawns + clears config).

```scheme
(define (transition-tick state)
  (let ((phase (car state))
        (frame (cadr state)))
    (cond
      ((and (eq? phase 'a) (>= frame 100))
       (scene/clear)
       (scene/load scene-b)
       (list 'b 0))
      ((and (eq? phase 'b) (>= frame 100))
       (list 'done frame))
      (else
       (world/step)
       (list phase (+ frame 1))))))

(define (setup)
  (world/reset!)
  (scene/load scene-a)
  (list 'a 0))

(big-bang (setup)
  (list 'on-tick transition-tick)
  (list 'stop-when (lambda (state) (eq? (car state) 'done))))
```

**State is now `(phase frame)`**: starts `'a 0`, transitions to `'b 0` at frame 100, stops at `'done`.

[VISUAL: Same as Example 13.8, but without canvas clear between phases — entities vanish/appear smoothly.]

<!-- BUILD: wire Example 13.9 (inline above) runnable; ensure scene/clear works. -->

---

## 13.5 Spawn Grids and Patterns

Spawning one-by-one is tedious. **`scene/spawn-many`** and **`scene/grid`** spawn prefabs in bulk.

### Example 13.9: A Grid of Wanderers

```scheme
(prefab/define 'wanderer
  (lambda (x y sprite speed radius)
    (let ((id (world/spawn x y 'wanderer)))
      (entity/sprite! id sprite)
      (ai/wander id radius 1.0)
      (entity/max-speed! id speed)
      id)))

(define (setup)
  (world/reset!)
  (scene/grid 'wanderer 4.0 4.0 4 3 4.0 4.0
              'blossom-1 0.3 0.5)
  0)

(big-bang (setup)
  (list 'on-tick (lambda (n)
             (world/step)
             (+ n 1)))
  (list 'stop-when (lambda (n) (>= n 200))))
```

**`(scene/grid prefab x0 y0 cols rows dx dy ...args)`**:
- Spawns `(* cols rows)` instances of `prefab`.
- Top-left at `(x0, y0)`, spaced `dx` apart horizontally, `dy` vertically.
- Each gets `...args` as remaining parameters.

Here: 4 columns, 3 rows, spacing 4.0×4.0 → 12 wanderers in a grid.

[VISUAL: A 4×3 grid of blossom-1 sprites, all wandering within their local neighborhoods.]

<!-- BUILD: wire Example 13.9 runnable; implement scene/grid as a loop over prefab/spawn. -->

---

### Example 13.10: Varied Grid

Pass a list of sprites instead of a single one; `scene/grid` cycles through them.

```scheme
(define (setup)
  (world/reset!)
  (scene/grid 'wanderer 4.0 4.0 4 3 4.0 4.0
              (list 'blossom-1 'blossom-5 'blossom-9)
              0.3 0.5)
  0)

(big-bang (setup)
  (list 'on-tick (lambda (n)
             (world/step)
             (+ n 1)))
  (list 'stop-when (lambda (n) (>= n 200))))
```

**Result:** First row: blossom-1, blossom-5, blossom-9, blossom-1. Second row: blossom-5, blossom-9, blossom-1, blossom-5. Third row: blossom-9, blossom-1, blossom-5, blossom-9.

[VISUAL: A 4×3 grid, flowers cycling through three types.]

<!-- BUILD: wire Example 13.10 runnable; ensure scene/grid accepts lists for cycled params. -->

